    "personal_information": "Nimit Narayani\nnimitnarayani@gmail.com\n+91 8126878372\nBangalore\nLinkedIn",
    "experience": "PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nConsulting Engineer, Cisco\n08/2022 – present | Bangalore, India\nIndian Air Force – Network Automation (Air-Gapped): Implemented Python automation in an on-site air-gapped environment to detect configuration and service issues across BGP, IS-IS, OSPF, MPLS, and L3VPN, reducing troubleshooting time by 80%. •Microsoft Data Center – Data Center Network: Configured Cisco NCS540 routers, handling provisioning, hardware validation, OSPF testing, and reachability checks before production integration. •Reliance Jio – Network Migration & Automation: Migrated 500+ devices from Juniper and Huawei to NCS540, supporting IS-IS and BGP. Validated configurations and built Python-based pre/ post migration checks for 1000+ devices, reducing verification time by 90%. •NIC Guwahati – Hardware Validation and P2P testing: Performed NRFU and hardware testing of network devices and supported deployment and performance validation. •MTNL India – Migration: Supported migration of 100+ sites to ASR and NCS routers, assisting with troubleshooting and validation of BGP, MPLS, L2/ L3 VPN, and VRF services. •Railway Telecom – Network Design: Assisted in on-site network design in coordination with customers and solution architects. •MTN South Africa – Migration Documentation: Prepared MOP documents for large-scale, multi-site migrations involving 50 routers, covering VPN, MPLS, OSPF, and IS-IS, including pre-check and rollback procedures. •Core-42 – Deployment Automation: Automated document validation, NIP vs live configuration checks, and bulk configuration deployment, reducing rollout time by 90%. •Network Automation Tool (Cisco In-Built Tool): Planned automation of CRD, DDD, NIP, and NRFU workflows to reduce manual effort by 80% and standardize deployments. •Pre/Post Comparison Tool: Automated pre- and post-migration checks to compare router configurations, interface states, and BGP/ OSPF adjacencies. 01/2022 – 07/2022 | Bangalore, India\nTechnical Undergraduate Intern, Cisco\nCompleted technical training and assisted with configuration, testing, and basic troubleshooting of network devices across 5–10 routers under engineer supervision.\nAI-ML virtual internship, AWS Academy\n10/2021 – 12/2021 | Delhi, India\nTrained & implemented AI-ML models through which we can solve real world problems.",
    "skills": "SKILLS\nPython\nNetworking (MPLS, OSPF, ISIS, BGP, IPv4, IPv6, TCP/IP, UDP)\nCisco IOS XR/XE\nDHCP\nDNS\nNetwork Automation (Troubleshooting/Configuration of Cisco IOS XR/XE devices)",
    "certifications": "CERTIFICATES\nAutomate The Boring Stuff With Python\nPython 3\nDevnet, Cisco\nCCNA (CISCO)",
    "education": "EDUCATION\nBachelor of Technology in Computer Science, Galgotias University 7.18/ 10 CGPA (First Division)\n2018 – 2022 | Noida, India",
